 "notes": "Solid black 'Leo T gas temp.' curve from Fig. 4 (ALP DM a->gamma gamma), the paper's main/nominal result with observed Leo T gas temperature (T_gas=6100 K, sigma_v=7.1 km/s); the dashed curve is the conservative T_gas=7552 K variant and is not reported. Curve recovered from vector paths in the e-print figures/Axion.pdf and calibrated against the log tick labels (m_a: 5-1000+ eV; g_agamma: 1e-15 to 1e-9 GeV^-1). Curve clipped to the plotted frame (m_a ~ 27 eV to 2.5 keV); sharp left cutoff at m_a ~ 27 eV corresponds to E_gamma = m_a/2 = 13.6 eV HI ionization threshold. The blue G33.4-8.0 MW gas-cloud curve was not used. Bounds derived from Lagrangian L = -(g_agamma/4) a F Ftilde (Eq. 11) with Gamma_a = m_a^3 g_agamma^2/(64 pi) (Eq. 12); the ALP is assumed to be all of the DM and the limit is set by requiring DM decay heating <= radiative cooling of Leo T gas (not a statistical confidence level; no CL stated, hence null). Limit depends on the Leo T DM halo density profile (Burkert profile from FSM13/Fig.1), not a single local DM density, so dm_density_assumed is null.",
